The fix is written, tested and queued to land on main, but it hadn't merged by the end of my time, so #554 stays open and the next run finishes it.

**Cause.** `images/base.Dockerfile` started from `rust:X-trixie`. That image is `buildpack-deps:trixie`, which installs `imagemagick`, `libmagickcore-dev` and `libmagickwand-dev`. Those pull in `libopenexr-dev` and `libopenexr-3-1-30` 3.1.13-2, plus about two hundred other packages nothing here uses (X11, cairo, mysql, svn, hg, …).

**What changed (branch commit `dfba380b`, queued with the manager):**
- **Ask 1:** the base image now starts from `rust:X-slim-trixie`, so OpenEXR is dropped, not excepted.
- **Ask 2:**
  - Each image installs its apt packages from a declared list, `images/base.packages` and `images/build.packages`.
  - A new check, `images/packages-check.sh` (shipped as `tacplus-packages-check`), is the last step of each image's build and runs again in `tacplus-smoke`. It fails if an installed package is not declared, part of Debian's base system, or a dependency of those. It also fails if a declared package is missing.
  - `scripts/images-plan.sh` now rebuilds an image when its list or the check changes.
  - New tests: `TestImagesPackagesCheck`, `TestImagesInstallTheirDeclaredPackages` and three `TestImagesPlan` cases. All fail without the change.
  - This run's own container is the published build image. Against its real package database the check names exactly the `buildpack-deps` packages, OpenEXR among them. Once `buildpack-deps`' own lists are added as declared, it passes on all 494 packages.
- **Ask 3:** no patch was cut from main: main has taken features since v2.6.1, and `v2.6.2` already exists on `release/2.6`. Instead there are seven draft backport PRs, all with green CI. Each names the tag to cut once it merges:

| PR | Branch | Tag |
|---|---|---|
| #555 | `release/2.0` | `v2.0.28` |
| #556 | `release/2.1` | `v2.1.21` |
| #557 | `release/2.2` | `v2.2.18` |
| #558 | `release/2.3` | `v2.3.20` |
| #559 | `release/2.4` | `v2.4.20` |
| #560 | `release/2.5` | `v2.5.21` |
| #561 | `release/2.6` | `v2.6.10` |

  2.0 needed more than the others. Its base used to take the C toolchain from `buildpack-deps`, so its list adds `build-essential`, `procps`, `xz-utils` and `zlib1g-dev`.

**Gates.** All 16 gates in `just gates` passed except `w2s-validate`, which failed on the first run. Two Rust tests got the same port (`AddrInUse`) because the fixture picks a free port, releases it, then binds it again later. Run alone on the same tree it passed. I filed the race as #562; it is the same bug as #531.

**Not verified:** no image was actually built, because Docker wasn't reachable in this run. The new images first build in the GitHub Actions images workflow: on main once this lands, and on each release line once its PR merges and the tag is cut. If a gate turns out to need a package `buildpack-deps` used to provide, that build or its smoke test fails there, and the package goes into the image's list.

**Trace (rule 13):** no handler is touched. `looper-trace check` reports only the findings already filed as #311.

**Left for the next run:** read the manager's verdict (and land again if it failed), put main's commit hash in the PR bodies and mark them ready, post the outcome comment, and close #554. Progress comments and a checkpoint are already on the issue and branch.
